.TH BIGNUMS 3 "2026-09-21" "BigNums" "Library Functions Manual"
.nr HY 0
.ds AD l
.SH NAME
bignums, BigInt, BigFloat \- fixed-capacity integer and binary float types
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include \(dqbignums.h\(dq
.PP
#define MAX_LIMBS 128
.PP
typedef struct {
    uint32_t limbs[MAX_LIMBS];
    int size;
} BigInt;
.PP
typedef struct {
    BigInt mantissa;
    int32_t exp;
    int sign;
} BigFloat;
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
BigNums stores numbers directly in fixed arrays of 32-bit limbs.
The integer capacity and maximum float mantissa size are 4096 bits.
The library is experimental and does not provide unbounded storage.
.SS BigInt
An unsigned integer has value equal to the sum of
limbs[i] * 2^(32*i), for 0 <= i < size.
The least significant limb comes first, independently of machine byte order.
The size must be between 1 and MAX_LIMBS.
In canonical form the highest active limb is nonzero, except that zero is
represented by size 1 and limbs[0] equal to zero.
Inactive limbs do not contribute to the value.
.SS BigFloat
A signed binary float has value sign * mantissa * 2^exp.
The sign is 1 or \-1; exp counts bits, not limbs or decimal places.
Normalized nonzero mantissas have bit 31 set in their highest active limb.
Canonical zero has a zero mantissa, exp 0, and sign 1.
Equivalent values can have different mantissa widths.
.SS Ownership
Both types contain their own storage and may be copied by structure assignment.
They need no caller-side allocation or deallocation.
FFT operations allocate temporary buffers internally.
.SS Preconditions
Use constructors before passing inputs to arithmetic routines.
Pointers must be non-NULL and size fields must be valid.
A distinct output generally need not be initialized.
Only rely on input/output aliasing when the particular function documents it.
There is no general pointer, range, or representation validation.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Most arithmetic routines return 0 on success and INT_MAX or \-1 on failure.
Comparisons, bit lookup, and scalar division/modulo return values instead of
ordinary status codes; consult their pages.
Errors may leave partially modified outputs.
No errno-based error reporting contract is provided.
Include <limits.h> to use INT_MAX.
.SH NOTES
Only bignums.h is needed by applications using the number API.
The FFT header has no required inclusion order.
The clz32 and next_pow2 helpers are private implementation details and are
not part of the installed header API.
.SH BUGS
The library has finite capacity, lossy float exponent alignment, incomplete
exponent-overflow checking, and limitations in decimal float printing.
See the individual function pages for applicable restrictions.
